- Diatonic scales (7 notes) use each letter once, in order, starting from tonic letter. So for intervals that form diatonic scales, next letter = previous letter +1 
mod7. Accidental determined by pitch class.
- Chromatic scales use all 12 notes, often with repeated letters (C, C#, D, D#...). But chromatic(tonic) can be handled separately by preferred chromatic 
representation.
- Non-diatonic scales like harmonic minor, enigmatic, pentatonic, octatonic, hexatonic may skip letters or repeat. Need heuristic.

