Thus parser:
```
fn parse_pitch(tonic: &str) -> Option<u8> {
    let mut chars = tonic.chars();
    let first = chars.next()?;
    let letter = match first.to_ascii_uppercase() { 'C'=>0, ... };
    let accidental = if tonic.len() > 1 {
        match tonic.chars().last() {
            Some('#') => 1,
            Some('b') => -1,
            _ => 0,
        }
    } else { 0 };
    Some((letter as i8 + accidental).rem_euclid(12) as u8)
}
```
But `tonic.len()` is bytes, for ASCII okay. Note names are ASCII. If tonic has trailing spaces? no.

