Applied edit to PalindromeCalculator.java
response:
The method needs to iterate over all factor pairs `(i, j)` within the range where `i <= j`, compute their product, check if it's a palindrome, and group the factor pairs by product value in a `TreeMap` (which implements `SortedMap`).

PalindromeCalculator.java
```
import java.util.*;

class PalindromeCalculator {

    SortedMap<Long, List<List<Integer>>> getPalindromeProductsWithFactors(int minFactor, int maxFactor) {
        TreeMap<Long, List<List<Integer>>> result = new TreeMap<>();

        for (int i = minFactor; i <= maxFactor; i++) {
            for (int j = i; j <= maxFactor; j++) {
                long product = (long) i * j;
                if (isPalindrome(product)) {
                    result.computeIfAbsent(product, k -> new ArrayList<>()).add(Arrays.asList(i, j));
                }
            }
        }

        return result;
    }

    private boolean isPalindrome(long number) {
        String s = String.valueOf(number);
        int left = 0, right = s.length() - 1;
        while (left < right) {
            if (s.charAt(left) != s.charAt(right)) return false;
            left++;
            right--;
        }
        return true;
    }

}
```
